e abnormal connections.\",2\r\n12472,POIC,\"Pseudoobstrucción intestinal crónica (POIC) is a rare and severe disorder that simulates intestinal obstruction without a fixed anatomical cause. It is characterized by chronic symptoms such as abdominal pain and vomiting, which can lead to significant issues with intestinal motility. Due to its nonspecific symptoms, POIC often results in a long diagnostic delay, necessitating a high level of suspicion and the exclusion of mechanical obstruction for accurate diagnosis. The condition can severely impact patients' nutritional status, often requiring nutritional support and specific management strategies. Additionally, POIC is sometimes associated with Short Bowel Syndrome, highlighting the need for education and tailored nutritional care for affected individuals.\",14\r\n12461,NUTRICIÓN EN CROHN'S DISEASE,,2\r\n11630,TOMOGRAFÍA COMPUTARIZADA,\"Tomografía Computarizada, commonly known as computed tomography (CT), is a sophisticated medical imaging technique that provides detailed information about the body's internal structures. It is particularly valuable in critical care settings, offering insights into body composition for critically ill patients. This imaging method is instrumental in diagnosing a variety of medical conditions. For instance, it is used to confirm the diagnosis of pancreatitis, assess its severity and complications, and study mesenteric pathology, including the diagnosis of intra-abdominal collections. Additionally, high-resolution computed tomography (HRCT) serves as a specialized diagnostic tool for confirming bronchiectasis and evaluating structural changes in the lungs. Overall, Tomografía Computarizada is essential for creating comprehensive images of internal organs, aiding in the diagnosis and management of numerous health issues.\",5\r\n2258,DIETA BAJA EN GRASA,\"The \"\"DIETA BAJA EN GRASA\"\" is a dietary approach that is recommended to optimize intestinal motility, particularly for patients experiencing digestive issues. This diet is especially beneficial for individuals with Crohn's disease who are dealing with steatorrhea, as it suggests a modification in the intake of triglycerides. By focusing on low-fat food options, this diet aims to alleviate symptoms and improve overall digestive health.\",2\r\n7869,SUPLEMENTOS,\"Los suplementos, que incluyen hierro, ácido fólico, calcio y vitaminas, son productos esenciales utilizados para aumentar la ingesta de nutrientes necesarios, especialmente en pacientes con POIC (Pérdida Ósea Inducida por Cáncer) y en poblaciones con dietas restrictivas o deficiencias confirmadas. Estos suplementos son fundamentales para prevenir deficiencias nutricionales y asegurar una adecuada salud y bienestar en estos grupos vulnerables.\",2\r\n12480,ADAPTATION,\"Adaptation is a biological process where the remaining intestine adjusts to take over the functions of the lost intestine, enhancing nutrient absorption.\",3\r\n4924,TEDUGLUTIDE,\"TEDUGLUTIDE is a medication currently under investigation for the treatment of intestinal failure, specifically targeting conditions such as Short Bowel Syndrome. It works by promoting intestinal adaptation, which enhances the absorption of nutrients in the intestines. This mechanism helps to reduce the reliance on parenteral nutrition in patients suffering from intestinal failure, thereby improving their overall nutritional status and quality of life.\",3\r\n9664,INTESTINE,\"The intestine is a crucial component of the digestive system, playing a significant role in the absorption of nutrients, which is essential for overall nutrition. Additionally, the intestine is involved in gluconeogenesis, contributing to the production of glucose in the body. However, it is important to note that the intestine can also be a site of inflammation and damage in individuals with celiac disease, where gluten triggers adverse reactions. Thus, the health of the intestine is vital not only for nutrient absorption and glucose production but also for preventing inflammatory conditions related to dietary components.\",2\r\n12517,ACIDOSIS D-LÁCTICA,\"Acidosis D-láctica is a significant complication in patients with SIC, resulting from the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates by Lactobacillus.\",1\r\n12515,DAPTOMICINA,Daptomicina is an antibiotic that is effective against biofilms formed on central venous catheters and is used in the treatment of infections related to these catheters.,1\r\n12514,EHAFI,\"EHAFI refers to a condition that requires specific prophylactic measures to be applied in patients, particularly in the context of nutritional support and lipid administration.\",1\r\n12519,FISTULA ARTERIOVENOSA,\"An arteriovenous fistula may be beneficial for some patients for the administration of NPD, providing an alternative access route.\",1\r\n12479,INTENSIVE NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT,Intensive nutritional support is a treatment approach for patients with intestinal failure to maintain nutritional status and prevent malnutrition.,1\r\n12487,TRÁNSITO INTESTINAL,Tránsito intestinal is a diagnostic procedure involving the use of contrast to assess the length of the remaining intestine and its functionality.,1\r\n12526,ALTERACIONES NUTRICIONALES,\"Nutritional imbalances that are common in patients with FEC, contributing to morbidity and mortality.\",1\r\n12530,DIETA POBRE EN RESIDUOS,\"A dietary approach recommended for patients with certain gastrointestinal conditions, aimed at reducing stool output.\",1\r\n12525,DRENAJES,\"Medical devices used to remove fluids from the body, which require careful monitoring in patients with FEC.\",1\r\n12529,DÉBITO,\"The output or flow rate from a fistula, which influences nutritional management decisions.\",1\r\n12521,SUSRUTA,\"An ancient Indian physician known as the father of medicine, who described treatments for entero-cutaneous fistulas in his work Susrutasamhit.\",1\r\n12528,OCTREÓTIDO,\"A medication used in the management of high-output fist